-galego","n":"Caldo galego","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Caldo galego or simply caldo (in Galician), also known as caldo gallego (in Spanish), meaning literally \"Galician broth\", is a traditional soup dish from Galicia. It is essentially a regional derivative (with added beans and turnip greens) of the very similar caldo verde, the traditional soup dish of neighbouring Portugal."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-caldo-galego"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caldo_galego"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Galician cuisine","cuisine/galician-cuisine"],["Spanish cuisine","cuisine/spanish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":10,"links":[["Bacon","ingredient/bacon"],["Cabbage","ingredient/cabbage"],["Chorizo","ingredient/chorizo"],["Lacón","ingredient/lacon"],["Phaseolus vulgaris","ingredient/phaseolus-vulgaris"],["Pig fat","ingredient/pig-fat"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Rapini","ingredient/rapini"],["White bean","ingredient/white-bean"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Spain on a Fork","ref":"site/spainonafork-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"spainonafork.com","note":"Albert Bevia's video channel and site of traditional and everyday Spanish recipes.","url":"https://spainonafork.com/welcome2/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Galician cuisine","links":[["Androlla","dish/androlla"],["Embutido","dish/embutido"],["Lacón","dish/lacon"],["Polbo á feira","dish/polbo-a-feira"],["Tarta de Santiago","dish/tarta-de-santiago"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/8/8b/Caldo_galego%2C_Galiza.jpg/500px-Caldo_galego%2C_Galiza.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Juan","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caldo_galego%2C_Galiza.jpg"}},"dish/filomena-ristorante":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/filomena-ristorante","n":"Filomena Ristorante","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Italian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Filomena Ristorante is an Italian-American restaurant located in the historic neighborhood of Georgetown in Washington, D.C.  It opened along Washington's C&O Canal in 1983. Fresh pasta is made by Filomena's ‘Pasta Mamas’ in the storefront kitchen. They greet patrons as they enter the restaurant."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-filomena-ristorante"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filomena_Ristorante"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pasta Grannies","ref":"site/pastagrannies-substack-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pastagrannies.substack.com","note":"Vicky Bennison's long-running video series filming Italian grandmothers making regional pasta by hand.","url":"https://pastagrannies.substack.com/p/pasta-grannies-is-now-on-substack","suggested":true},{"name":"Recipes from Italy","ref":"site/recipesfromitaly-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"recipesfromitaly.com","note":"Traditional Italian recipes written by Italian home cooks, organized by region and course.","url":"https://recipesfromitaly.com","suggested":true},{"name":"Manu's Menu","ref":"site/manusmenu-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"manusmenu.com","note":"Italian-born home cook Manuela sharing classic family and regional Italian dishes.","url":"https://www.manusmenu.com/about/about-this-site","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Italian cuisine","links":[["8½ Otto e Mezzo Bombana","dish/8-otto-e-mezzo-bombana"],["A16 (restaurant)","dish/a16-restaurant"],["Acquacotta","dish/acquacotta"],["Agliata","dish/agliata"],["Agnolotti","dish/agnolotti"],["Alfredo alla Scrofa","dish/alfredo-alla-scrofa"],["Alioto's","dish/alioto-s"],["Amalfi's Italian Restaurant","dish/amalfi-s-italian-restaurant"],["Amato's","dish/amato-s"],["Angel